+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:11+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#athena","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Athena","description":"Amazon Athena","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:01:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#ai-ml","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Machine Learning \u0026 AI","description":"Machine Learning \u0026 AI","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:22+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#industry#healthcare-lifesciences","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#industry","name":"healthcare-lifesciences","description":"\u003cp\u003eThis tag is initially being created specifically for the Directory Cards componenet on aws.amazon.com/health/case-studies/. When the GCRP decided to add multilingual content to the CSDIR in 2023, the owners of this page only wanted to display the English content in our Directory. Because the Directory Cards component on their page uses an OR operator to pull in content from two tags, they would be unable to add a prefilter condition to look for only English content. This can only be done if the page is using an AND operator. Thus, this tag will be autoapplied to all content that meets the current prefilter conditions. At that point, the page owners can use the AND operator to display content with this tag and GLOBAL#language#english.\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2023-04-26T20:23:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-04-26T20:23:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#skyalert-en-from-es-directory","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"skyalert-en-from-es-directory","dateCreated":"2024-02-03T03:47:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-02-06T01:35:37+0000","additionalFields":{"descriptionSummary":"SkyAlert is an innovative technology company that quickly alerts millions of people living in earthquake-prone areas, promoting a culture of prevention against natural disasters. In order to provide customers—both businesses and individuals—with the right tools to protect them during earthquakes, SkyAlert migrated its infrastructure from Microsoft Azure to Amazon Web Services (AWS). After implementing its Internet of Things (IoT) solution to run on AWS and its efficient alert service, SkyAlert scales quickly and can send millions of messages in a few seconds, helping to save lives in the event of earthquakes.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/skyalert_logo%401x.27b39f5ae8919cd5eac26ac7e8af6df26e3df29d.png","displayLocation":"Mexico","customerNameLower":"skyalert","footerInfoText":"Published Date","industry":"Manufacturing","sortDate":"2023-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/skyalert/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"SkyAlert","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2023","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"SkyAlert Helps Save Lives from Natural Disasters Using AWS Solutions"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#industry#manufacturing","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#industry","name":"Manufacturing","description":"Manufacturing","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:42:32+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:06+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#iot","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Internet of Things (IoT)","description":"Internet of Things (IoT)","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-08-22T20:28:39+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#big-data-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Big Data \u0026 Analytics","description":"Big Data \u0026 Analytics","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:31:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-19T05:00:36+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#lambda","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"AWS Lambda","description":"AWS Lambda","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:04:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32